WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.819
Trace the installed branch from its
defined source to the vessel

2
00:00:03.939 --> 00:00:06.947
connection against the controlled piping
diagram.

3
00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:09.499
Check the specified route, isolation

4
00:00:09.619 --> 00:00:12.157
and identifiers using safe methods.

5
00:00:12.277 --> 00:00:15.264
Do not assume a pipe has the intended
contents

6
00:00:15.384 --> 00:00:17.384
because its colour looks familiar.

7
00:00:17.504 --> 00:00:21.963
A label and the actual connection must
agree with the system information.

8
00:00:22.583 --> 00:00:25.399
For fixed pipework, contents
identification

9
00:00:25.519 --> 00:00:28.697
and applicable flow direction help prevent
mistakes.

10
00:00:28.817 --> 00:00:31.935
Compare labels with the route and
controlled drawing,

11
00:00:32.055 --> 00:00:34.252
including places where lines cross.

12
00:00:34.372 --> 00:00:38.682
A correct label on the wrong connected
branch remains a discrepancy.

13
00:00:38.802 --> 00:00:41.255
Record the location so the engineering

14
00:00:41.375 --> 00:00:43.807
team can resolve the actual connection

15
00:00:43.927 --> 00:00:46.221
rather than merely replacing the label.

16
00:00:46.841 --> 00:00:48.959
The branch may be installed as drawn

17
00:00:49.079 --> 00:00:52.983
while the required utility-quality
evidence is still unavailable.

18
00:00:53.103 --> 00:00:55.364
Record those as separate statuses.

19
00:00:55.484 --> 00:00:58.364
A pressure indication alone cannot
establish

20
00:00:58.484 --> 00:01:01.556
chemical or microbiological suitability.

21
00:01:01.676 --> 00:01:04.940
Determine what qualification and sampling
evidence

22
00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:08.942
applies to the intended use through the
approved project approach,

23
00:01:09.062 --> 00:01:12.817
rather than borrowing limits from an
unrelated sterile process.

24
00:01:13.437 --> 00:01:16.168
A late branch addition may affect the
upstream

25
00:01:16.288 --> 00:01:18.762
system as well as the receiving vessel.

26
00:01:18.882 --> 00:01:21.314
Identify the changed configuration

27
00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:23.802
and assess the required installation

28
00:01:23.922 --> 00:01:26.077
and other verification before use.

29
00:01:26.197 --> 00:01:28.800
Do not assume that the original utility

30
00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:32.034
qualification covers every future
extension.

31
00:01:32.154 --> 00:01:34.154
Our workbook asks which records

32
00:01:34.275 --> 00:01:38.797
and responsible system owners must be
linked before closing the interface.
